# Lumenhold Academy — 简体中文 (zh-CN) translation of content/events/people_students.grim
# Maintained by `node tools/grim.js i18n zh-CN`. Translate the text after "="; keep {tokens}.
# "# en:" shows the English source. [hash] marks the English version a line was translated from;
# lines marked STALE need updating — after fixing the text, delete the [hash] and re-run the tool.


@event lyra_intro
# en: The Last Copy
title [370a21] = 最后一本
# en: You reach for the last copy of "Foundations of Flame" and a ringed hand gets there first. "I need it more," says a tall girl with crimson hair, not looking at you. "You'll only underline the wrong bits."
text [81419e] = 你伸手去拿最后一本《火焰基础》，一只戴戒指的手抢先了一步。“我更需要它，”一个高挑的红发女孩说，看都没看你，“你只会划错重点。”
# en: Two hands reaching for the same red-bound book on a library shelf; one hand wears a signet ring with a flame crest.
scene [396ae6] = 两只手伸向图书馆书架上同一本红皮书；其中一只手上戴着刻有火焰家徽的印章戒指。
# en: Let her have it
opt.left.label [6e7c4e] = 让给她
# en: "At least you know your place," she says, which is somehow worse than rudeness. Lyra Vaneshade. Everyone knows the name.
opt.left.say.1 [69ebd2] = “至少你有自知之明。”她说，这不知怎么比无礼更伤人。莱拉·凡妮希德。人人都知道这个名字。
# en: Argue for it
opt.right.label [503eb7] = 据理力争
# en: You quote chapter three at her. She raises an eyebrow, then hands you the book. "Fine. Return it underlined correctly."
opt.right.say.1 [bbdc0c] = 你给她背了一段第三章。她挑起眉毛，然后把书递给了你。“行。还的时候把重点划对。”
# en: She wins the argument in four sentences and leaves with the book. You think of the perfect comeback that night.
opt.right.say.2 [b0bbf8] = 她四句话就赢了这场争论，拿着书走了。那天晚上你才想到完美的回嘴。

@event lyra_letter
# en: A Letter With a Black Seal
title [47420d] = 黑色封印的信
# en: You find Lyra on a window seat with a crumpled letter. Black seal. Her family's. She's not crying; Vaneshades don't. But she's not quite not crying either.
text [4caeea] = 你发现莱拉坐在窗台上，手里攥着一封揉皱的信。黑色封印。她家族的。她没有哭；凡妮希德家的人不哭。但她也不完全是没在哭。
# en: A girl sitting on a window seat in an empty corridor, crushing a letter with a black wax seal in her fist, face turned away.
scene [ed4b56] = 空荡荡的走廊里，一个女孩坐在窗台上，把一封黑蜡封口的信攥在拳中，脸转向一边。
# en: Pretend you didn't see
opt.left.label [25b345] = 假装没看见
# en: You walk past. Later, she's flawless again, as if nothing happened. Maybe nothing did.
opt.left.say.1 [8cb435] = 你走了过去。后来，她又是那个无懈可击的她了，仿佛什么都没发生。也许真的什么都没发生。
# en: Sit down beside her
opt.right.label [e6df6e] = 在她身边坐下
# en: "Second place," she says eventually. "I came second in the Winter Trials. My mother wants to know who beat me." She almost laughs. "It's always someone."
opt.right.say.1 [2ea3fc] = “第二名，”她终于开口，“我在冬季考核里拿了第二。我母亲想知道是谁赢了我。”她几乎笑了出来。“总会有那么一个人。”

@event lyra_study_rivalry
# en: Top of the Class
title [76842e] = 全班第一
# en: The professors post this week's rankings, with an open paper this afternoon for anyone who wants to improve their place. Lyra is first{&. You're close enough to see the back of her head.|, again. You're close enough to read her handwriting.|. Of course she is. You're one name below her, which is somehow worse than three.} She notices you noticing.
text [f904e6] = 教授们公布了本周排名，还说今天下午有一场公开考试，想提高名次的人都可以参加。莱拉第一{&。你离她近到能看见她的后脑勺。|，又是第一。你离她近到能看清她的笔迹。|。当然是她。你就排在她下面一名，这不知怎么比差三名还难受。}她注意到了你在注意她。
# en: Two students at opposite ends of a long library table, surrounded by towers of books, glaring over the tops of them.
scene [e05ebb] = 长长的图书馆桌两端各坐一个学生，被一摞摞书包围着，隔着书堆互相瞪视。
# en: Suggest studying together
opt.left.label [d07df2] = 提议一起学习
# en: {&"Together?" She considers this like a foreign custom. Then she pulls out a chair. She's an excellent, merciless study partner.|She already has two cups of tea and your chair pulled out. "You're late," she says. You aren't.|"Fine. But I'm quizzing you first." She is merciless again, and you're better for it.}
opt.left.say.1 [a3ad5c] = {&“一起？”她像在考虑一种外国习俗。然后她拉出了一把椅子。她是个出色而无情的学习搭档。|她已经备好了两杯茶，把你的椅子也拉了出来。“你迟到了，”她说。你并没有。|“行。但我先考你。”她又一次毫不留情，而你因此进步了。}
# en: Beat her outright
opt.right.label [7983cc] = 正面击败她
# en: The afternoon paper puts you first. Lyra stares at the list for a long time. Then she finds you and says, "Good." She means it.
opt.right.say.1 [8e7fb5] = 下午的考试让你排到了第一。莱拉盯着名单看了很久。然后她找到你，说：“很好。”她是认真的。
# en: {&You cram through lunch and come third. Lyra is still first. She doesn't gloat. That's worse.|Second, by one mark. Lyra leaves a note on your desk: "Close." You keep it.|You come fourth. Lyra looks almost disappointed on your behalf, which is unbearable.}
opt.right.say.2 [1024cc] = {&你午饭时间都在临阵磨枪，结果是第三。莱拉还是第一。她没有得意。这更糟。|第二，差一分。莱拉在你桌上留了张字条：“很接近。”你把它收了起来。|你排第四。莱拉看上去几乎在替你失望，这简直让人受不了。}

@event lyra_family_gala
# en: The Vaneshade Winter Gala
title [cc6875] = 凡妮希德冬季晚宴
# en: "My family's winter gala," Lyra says, too casually. "I need a guest who won't embarrass me. You'll do. Probably. You'll need proper clothes."
text [f5575c] = “我家的冬季晚宴，”莱拉说，语气太过随意，“我需要一个不会让我丢脸的客人。你还行。大概。你得穿得像样点。”
# en: A glittering ballroom in a noble house, candles floating in mid-air, a tall woman in crimson watching the crowd like a hawk.
scene [bf8dd3] = 贵族宅邸里金碧辉煌的舞厅，蜡烛悬浮在空中，一位身着深红衣裙的高挑女人像鹰一样注视着人群。
# en: Decline
opt.left.label [eaef39] = 拒绝
# en: "Of course." A pause. "It doesn't matter." It clearly does.
opt.left.say.1 [1fe8ea] = “当然。”停顿。“无所谓。”显然有所谓。
# en: Go with her (15 gold for clothes)
opt.right.label [e8a9e8] = 陪她去（置装花费 15 金币）
# en: Lyra's mother asks who your parents are, and then asks no further questions at all. Lyra squeezes your hand under the table, hard.
opt.right.say.1 [3ae20f] = 莱拉的母亲问起你父母是谁，然后就再也没有问别的了。莱拉在桌下用力握住了你的手。
# en: You dance, you charm a duke, you don't spill anything. In the carriage home, Lyra falls asleep on your shoulder.
opt.right.say.2 [db666b] = 你跳舞，你迷倒了一位公爵，你什么都没洒。回家的马车上，莱拉靠在你肩上睡着了。

@event lyra_confession
# en: Lyra Doesn't Lose
title [4e22c6] = 莱拉从不认输
# en: After practice, Lyra doesn't leave. "I don't lose," she says, staring at the scorch marks. "I don't. But I think — " She stops. Starts again. "I think I've lost to you. Say something before I set something on fire."
text [0b2d38] = 练习结束后，莱拉没有走。“我不会输，”她盯着地上的焦痕说，“我不会。但我觉得——”她停住了。又重新开口。“我觉得我输给你了。快说点什么，不然我要烧东西了。”
# en: A girl with crimson hair standing very close in a practice ring at dusk, sparks still drifting from her wand, cheeks flushed.
scene [fa1888] = 黄昏的练习圈里，一个红发女孩站得很近，魔杖上还飘着火星，脸颊泛红。
# en: Let her down gently
opt.left.label [c62f10] = 温柔地拒绝她
# en: She nods, sharp and quick. "Understood." She practises alone for a month. Then one day she nods to you in the corridor, and it's almost all right.
opt.left.say.1 [d294fb] = 她干脆利落地点了点头。“明白了。”她独自练了一个月。后来有一天她在走廊里朝你点点头，一切差不多都好了。
# en: Kiss her
opt.right.label [5fa79c] = 吻她
# en: Nothing catches fire. Well. Something does, but it's only the practice dummy, and neither of you notices for a while.
opt.right.say.1 [90be4c] = 什么都没着火。好吧。有东西着了，但只是练习用的假人，而且你们好一阵子都没注意到。

@event lyra_family_ultimatum
# en: The Ultimatum
title [f0d1f2] = 最后通牒
# en: Another black-sealed letter. Lyra reads it twice and goes white. "My mother has found out about us. End it, she says, or she ends my inheritance." She looks at you. "Tell me what to do."
text [fa5d3c] = 又一封黑色封印的信。莱拉读了两遍，脸色发白。“我母亲知道我们的事了。她说，要么断了，要么她断了我的继承权。”她看着你。“告诉我该怎么办。”
# en: Lyra holding a letter with a black seal, her other hand clenched around a ring she has just pulled off.
scene [8c7e83] = 莱拉手持一封黑色封印的信，另一只手紧紧攥着一枚刚摘下的戒指。
# en: "Choose yourself, not them."
opt.left.label [1f5be4] = “选择你自己，而不是他们。”
# en: She tears the letter in half. Then in quarters. Then she sets the quarters on fire and laughs like she hasn't in years.
opt.left.say.1 [3f7f4b] = 她把信撕成两半。再撕成四片。然后把碎片点着，笑得像好多年没这样笑过。
# en: "Easy for you to say," she snaps. She doesn't mean it. She also doesn't take it back.
opt.left.say.2 [66097c] = “说得轻巧。”她冲你吼道。她不是真心的。但她也没有收回这句话。
# en: She tears the letter in half. Then in quarters. Then she sets the quarters on fire and laughs like she hasn't in years.
opt.left.say.3 [3f7f4b] = 她把信撕成两半。再撕成四片。然后把碎片点着，笑得像好多年没这样笑过。
# en: "Easy for you to say," she snaps. She doesn't mean it. She also doesn't take it back.
opt.left.say.4 [66097c] = “说得轻巧。”她冲你吼道。她不是真心的。但她也没有收回这句话。
# en: Step back so she doesn't lose everything
opt.right.label [9c8862] = 退一步，让她不至于失去一切
# en: You end it before she has to. She doesn't argue. That's how you know how much it costs her.
opt.right.say.1 [27b1b0] = 在她不得不开口之前，你先结束了这段感情。她没有争辩。正因如此，你才知道这对她代价有多大。

@event lyra_rival_sabotage
# en: Sabotage in Class
title [1db464] = 课堂上的暗算
# en: Your perfect potion turns black and starts screaming. Across the room, Lyra is very carefully not looking at you.
text [8b133c] = 你那锅完美的药剂突然变黑，开始尖叫。教室另一头，莱拉非常小心地没往你这边看。
# en: A cauldron spitting black smoke, a crimson-haired student walking away with a tiny vial hidden in her sleeve.
scene [f64dbb] = 一口坩埚喷出黑烟，一个红发学生走开，袖子里藏着一只小瓶。
# en: Retaliate
opt.left.label [5cb1e8] = 报复回去
# en: Next lesson, her wand produces only bubbles. Pink ones. She knows. You both know. It's war. It's sort of fun.
opt.left.say.1 [6d8609] = 下节课，她的魔杖只能冒出泡泡。粉红色的。她知道。你们俩都知道。开战了。还挺好玩的。
# en: You're caught slipping something into her bag. She looks genuinely delighted.
opt.left.say.2 [7dfe71] = 你往她包里塞东西时被逮了个正着。她看起来真心高兴。
# en: Confront her directly
opt.right.label [eed285] = 当面质问她
# en: "That was beneath you." She flushes. "...Yes. It was." The next day there's a perfect replacement potion on your desk.
opt.right.say.1 [3c2fd2] = “这有失你的身份。”她脸红了。“……是。是有失身份。”第二天，你桌上放着一份完美的替代药剂。

@event lyra_burnout
# en: Lyra Falls
title [d0abf9] = 莱拉倒下了
# en: You find Lyra face-down on a library desk at dawn, not asleep — out cold. She's been studying for three days straight. "Don't tell anyone," she mumbles when she comes round. "Mother can't know."
text [794170] = 黎明时分你发现莱拉趴在图书馆的桌上，不是睡着了——是昏过去了。她已经连续学了三天。“别告诉任何人，”她醒过来时含糊地说，“不能让母亲知道。”
# en: A girl collapsed across a library desk among scattered notes, quill still in hand, candle burned down to nothing.
scene [91fdd5] = 一个女孩瘫倒在图书馆书桌上，周围散落着笔记，手里还握着羽毛笔，蜡烛已经燃尽。
# en: Take her to the infirmary anyway
opt.left.label [26e217] = 还是把她送去医务室
# en: She's furious. Then she sleeps for nineteen hours. When she wakes up, she says, quietly, "Thank you."
opt.left.say.1 [0d4dbd] = 她气坏了。然后她睡了十九个小时。醒来时，她轻声说：“谢谢你。”
# en: Cover for her and make her rest
opt.right.label [bfbbb0] = 替她打掩护，逼她休息
# en: You tell her professors she has a cold and sit by her door with your homework. She sleeps. You keep watch.
opt.right.say.1 [1b1d64] = 你告诉她的教授们她感冒了，然后带着作业守在她门口。她睡了。你守着。

@event tobias_intro
# en: The Lost Boy
title [3f2dc0] = 迷路的男孩
# en: A big, broad-shouldered boy is leading a crying first-year through the corridors. "Don't worry, I know exactly where the infirmary is," he says, and walks confidently into a broom cupboard.
text [03f851] = 一个高大宽肩的男生正领着一个哭鼻子的一年级生穿过走廊。“别担心，我很清楚医务室在哪儿。”他说着，满怀信心地走进了扫帚间。
# en: A large, gentle-faced boy leading a crying first-year by the hand down the wrong corridor, both very lost.
scene [0ae971] = 一个面容温和的大个子男生牵着一个哭泣的一年级生走在错误的走廊里，两人都迷路了。
# en: Point them the right way
opt.left.label [f53c4f] = 给他们指路
# en: "Ah. Left, you say. Right. I mean, correct." He grins, enormous and sheepish. "Tobias. Turnip scholarship. Thanks."
opt.left.say.1 [74c134] = “啊。你说左边。对。我是说，没错。”他咧嘴一笑，笑容大大的，有点不好意思。“托比亚斯。芜菁奖学金。谢啦。”
# en: Walk with them
opt.right.label [799c3a] = 陪他们一起走
# en: You end up taking the scenic route, and the first-year stops crying because Tobias is telling a very long story about a goat.
opt.right.say.1 [c5721c] = 你们最后绕了一条风景路线，一年级生不哭了，因为托比亚斯在讲一个关于山羊的超长故事。

@event tobias_homesick
# en: Homesick
title [a133e0] = 想家
# en: Tobias has gone quiet. He's planted seedlings in every cup in the common room. "Harvest at home," he says. "First one I've missed. Ma's doing it alone."
text [fd42a8] = 托比亚斯变得沉默了。他在公共休息室的每个杯子里都种了幼苗。“家里在收庄稼，”他说，“这是我第一次错过。我妈一个人在干。”
# en: A dormitory windowsill crowded with clay pots of seedlings, a big boy watering them with a tiny can.
scene [433f64] = 宿舍窗台上挤满了种着幼苗的陶盆，一个大个子男生正用一只小水壶浇水。
# en: Cheer him up with a joke
opt.left.label [c33487] = 讲个笑话逗他开心
# en: Your joke is terrible. He laughs anyway, the big rumbling laugh, and that seems to help.
opt.left.say.1 [e60401] = 你的笑话烂透了。他还是笑了，那种轰隆隆的大笑，好像真的管用。
# en: Help him build a window garden
opt.right.label [8aab52] = 帮他建一个窗台菜园
# en: You buy seeds and a stack of pots. By the end of the week the common room smells of tomato leaves. Tobias whistles while he waters them.
opt.right.say.1 [4f8881] = 你买来种子和一摞花盆。到周末，公共休息室里满是番茄叶的味道。托比亚斯浇水时吹着口哨。

@event tobias_bad_harvest
# en: The Harvest Failed
title [aab2ca] = 歉收
# en: Tobias is packing. Blight took the harvest. His family needs money, and hands. "Thirty crowns would get them through winter," he says, not asking. "But I haven't got thirty crowns. I've got two arms."
text [b3ac08] = 托比亚斯在收拾行李。枯萎病毁了收成。他家需要钱，也需要人手。“三十克朗就能让他们熬过冬天，”他说，并不是在开口要，“可我没有三十克朗。我只有两条胳膊。”
# en: A boy packing a battered trunk in an empty dormitory, a letter with smudged handwriting open on the bed.
scene [7cc0f7] = 空荡荡的宿舍里，一个男生在收拾一只破旧的行李箱，床上摊着一封字迹模糊的信。
# en: Persuade him to stay and find work here
opt.left.label [4e1985] = 劝他留下，在这里找工作
# en: You walk him to the job board. He signs up for double shifts at the stables and sends every crown home. He stays.
opt.left.say.1 [3cac05] = 你陪他去了招工告示板。他报了马厩的双班，把每一枚克朗都寄回了家。他留下了。
# en: He listens, nods, and takes the barge in the morning. He's back in two months, thinner and quieter.
opt.left.say.2 [373ae1] = 他听着，点点头，第二天早上坐上了驳船。两个月后他回来了，瘦了，也更沉默了。
# en: Give him thirty crowns
opt.right.label [902ad2] = 给他三十克朗
# en: He tries to refuse three times. Then he hugs you so hard your spine cracks. "I'll pay you back. Every crown. Every one."
opt.right.say.1 [2214f7] = 他推辞了三次。然后抱住你，抱得你脊椎咔咔响。“我会还你的。每一枚克朗。每一枚。”

@event tobias_repays
# en: Every Crown
title [807b67] = 每一枚克朗
# en: A lumpy, hand-stitched pouch on your pillow: thirty crowns exactly, in small coins. And a jar of honey from home. A note in big, careful letters: "TOLD YOU. — T."
text [150790] = 你枕头上放着一只鼓鼓囊囊、手工缝制的小袋子：正好三十克朗，全是零钱。还有一罐家里的蜂蜜。一张字条，字写得又大又认真：“说到做到。——托”
# en: A clumsy hand-stitched pouch of coins and a jar of honey left on a dormitory pillow.
scene [1e69a7] = 宿舍枕头上一只笨拙的手缝钱袋和一罐蜂蜜。
# en: Smile
opt.ok.label [c2972f] = 笑一笑
# en: The honey tastes of a farm you have never seen and somehow already miss.
opt.ok.say.1 [8639ca] = 那罐蜂蜜尝起来像一座你从没见过、却已经开始想念的农场。

@event tobias_godparent
# en: The Mandrake Baby
title [5adaaf] = 曼德拉草宝宝
# en: Tobias presents a flowerpot containing a very small mandrake in a knitted hat. "This is Gerald," he says. "I'd like you to be his godparent." Gerald screams softly.
text [287127] = 托比亚斯捧出一个花盆，里面是一株戴着针织帽的小小曼德拉草。“这是杰拉尔德，”他说，“我想请你当他的教父母。”杰拉尔德轻声尖叫。
# en: A tiny mandrake in a pot wearing a knitted hat, a beaming boy presenting it like a newborn.
scene [39f8e3] = 一株戴着针织帽的小曼德拉草种在盆里，一个笑容灿烂的男生像捧着新生儿一样把它捧出来。
# en: Politely decline
opt.left.label [8a601d] = 礼貌地拒绝
# en: "No pressure," says Tobias, visibly pressured. Gerald glares at you from under his hat.
opt.left.say.1 [00f5a4] = “没压力的。”托比亚斯说，明显压力很大。杰拉尔德从帽子底下瞪着你。
# en: Accept with honour
opt.right.label [395d80] = 荣幸地接受
# en: You are now Gerald's godparent. Gerald bites you. Tobias says this means Gerald loves you.
opt.right.say.1 [95091f] = 你现在是杰拉尔德的教父母了。杰拉尔德咬了你一口。托比亚斯说这代表杰拉尔德爱你。

@event tobias_bullied
# en: Tobias and the Prefect
title [0d0b40] = 托比亚斯与级长
# en: Bram is doing an impression of Tobias's accent in the corridor. People are laughing. Tobias is pretending not to hear, ears burning red.
text [cf84da] = 布拉姆在走廊里模仿托比亚斯的口音。大家都在笑。托比亚斯假装没听见，耳朵红得发烫。
# en: A burly prefect mocking a big farm boy in a crowded corridor, students sniggering, the boy's ears bright red.
scene [d6b2fe] = 拥挤的走廊里，一个魁梧的级长在嘲笑一个高大的农家男孩，学生们在窃笑，男孩的耳朵通红。
# en: Stay out of it
opt.left.label [03d24a] = 不掺和
# en: Tobias doesn't mention it. He doesn't sit with you at dinner, either.
opt.left.say.1 [be0b18] = 托比亚斯没提这事。晚饭时他也没和你坐一起。
# en: Step in
opt.right.label [db9576] = 站出来
# en: "Funny," you say. "Do your father next." The laughter turns on Bram. He stalks off. Tobias stares at you in awe.
opt.right.say.1 [26c55a] = “真好笑，”你说，“下一个学你爸吧。”笑声转向了布拉姆。他气冲冲地走了。托比亚斯敬畏地看着你。
# en: Bram turns his attention to you instead, with interest. Tobias brings you a pie later. A whole pie.
opt.right.say.2 [a956b8] = 布拉姆转而饶有兴趣地盯上了你。后来托比亚斯给你送来一个馅饼。一整个。

@event tobias_confession
# en: A Confession, With Vegetables
title [a19fc5] = 一场带着蔬菜的告白
# en: Tobias corners you in the greenhouse holding a very large pumpkin. "I grew this," he says. "For you. It's the best one. I didn't know how else to — I like you. Like that. I've practised this on the pumpkin. Sorry."
text [157367] = 托比亚斯抱着一个很大的南瓜在温室里拦住了你。“这是我种的，”他说，“送你的。是最好的那个。我不知道还能怎么——我喜欢你。是那种喜欢。我对着南瓜练习过了。对不起。”
# en: A big boy holding out a perfect pumpkin like an offering in a greenhouse, cheeks scarlet.
scene [563b87] = 温室里一个大个子男生像献礼一样捧出一个完美的南瓜，脸颊通红。
# en: Let him down gently
opt.left.label [b009f9] = 温柔地拒绝他
# en: He nods a lot. "That's all right. That's fine. You can still have the pumpkin." You keep it until it rots, out of loyalty.
opt.left.say.1 [f837ce] = 他拼命点头。“没关系。没事的。南瓜你还是可以留着。”出于情义，你一直留到它烂掉。
# en: Say yes
opt.right.label [c73ccb] = 答应他
# en: He drops the pumpkin. It's fine; pumpkins are sturdy. So, it turns out, are his hugs.
opt.right.say.1 [3f29ab] = 他手里的南瓜掉了。没事；南瓜很结实。事实证明，他的拥抱也是。

@event tobias_picnic
# en: A Picnic in the Orchard
title [2dff91] = 果园野餐
# en: Tobias has packed a picnic: {~bread he baked, cheese he begged from the kitchens, apples from the orchard he has befriended|a pie with your initials in the crust, slightly burnt, and a jar of honey from someone he helped|plums, hard cheese and something he calls a salad, which is mostly flowers}. "No {~exams|essays|professors} for six hours," he announces. "I checked."
text [70bc74] = 托比亚斯准备了野餐：{~他自己烤的面包，从厨房软磨硬泡来的奶酪，还有他“交了朋友”的果园里的苹果|一个酥皮上刻着你名字缩写的馅饼，有点烤焦了，还有一罐他帮过的人送的蜂蜜|李子、硬奶酪，还有一样他称为沙拉的东西，基本上全是花}。“六个小时内没有{~考试|论文|教授}，”他宣布，“我查过了。”
# en: A checked blanket under blossoming apple trees, a basket of bread and cheese, two students lying in the dappled light.
scene [66c097] = 开花的苹果树下铺着格子毯，一篮面包和奶酪，两个学生躺在斑驳的光影里。
# en: Bring your books anyway
opt.left.label [b8ab05] = 还是带上书
# en: You study on the blanket. He eyes the books, sighs a very small sigh, and falls asleep with his head in your lap. It's still lovely.
opt.left.say.1 [fcc2e1] = 你在毯子上学习。他瞄了一眼那些书，很轻很轻地叹了口气，然后枕着你的腿睡着了。依然很美好。
# en: Leave everything behind
opt.right.label [1ca23f] = 把一切都抛在脑后
# en: The afternoon goes golden and slow. You can't remember the last time you didn't think about grades.
opt.right.say.1 [5c67d2] = 午后变得金黄而缓慢。你已经记不起上一次不去想成绩是什么时候了。

@event seraphine_intro
# en: Your Left Shoe
title [0404ae] = 你的左脚鞋
# en: A girl drifts past you in the corridor and says, without stopping, "You're going to lose your left shoe today. Don't worry, it's under the stairs in the east wing."
text [01fffe] = 一个女孩从你身边飘过，头也不回地说：“你今天会丢一只左脚的鞋。别担心，它在东翼的楼梯底下。”
# en: A slight girl with silver-grey eyes and a scarf of stars passing in a corridor, pointing absently at someone's feet.
scene [c9cd41] = 一个纤瘦的女孩围着星星图案的围巾，长着银灰色的眼睛，在走廊里经过时漫不经心地指着某人的脚。
# en: Ignore her
opt.left.label [44f360] = 不理她
# en: That afternoon a staircase moves and eats your left shoe. It is, eventually, under the stairs in the east wing.
opt.left.say.1 [b13d26] = 那天下午，一道楼梯挪了位置，吃掉了你的左脚鞋。最终，它确实在东翼的楼梯底下。
# en: Ask how she knows
opt.right.label [48f36e] = 问她怎么知道的
# en: "I don't know things," she says. "Things know me." Then: "Seraphine. You'll want the shoe back by four." You get it back at 3:58.
opt.right.say.1 [ef5d82] = “我不知道事情，”她说，“是事情知道我。”然后又说：“瑟拉芬。你会想在四点前把鞋拿回来的。”你在三点五十八分拿了回来。

@event seraphine_tarot
# en: The Cards
title [c5101b] = 牌
# en: Seraphine shuffles a battered tarot deck. "One card," she says. "For you. Only if you want it. They're quite rude sometimes."
text [95625a] = 瑟拉芬洗着一副破旧的塔罗牌。“抽一张，”她说，“给你的。只要你想。它们有时候挺没礼貌的。”
# en: A tarot spread on a velvet cloth in candlelight, a girl's pale fingers turning over a card showing a lightning-struck tower.
scene [8a2f94] = 烛光下天鹅绒布上摊开的塔罗牌阵，一个女孩苍白的手指翻开一张画着雷击高塔的牌。
# en: Draw a card
opt.left.label [a80dc6] = 抽一张
# en: The Star. "Hope," she says, delighted. "And someone's going to tell you a secret. Oh — it's me. I like you." She blushes.
opt.left.say.1 [bfb1c6] = 星星。“希望，”她高兴地说，“还有人要告诉你一个秘密。噢——是我。我喜欢你。”她脸红了。
# en: The Tower. She looks at it a long time. "It's fine," she says. "Towers fall. That's what they're for."
opt.left.say.2 [ecbdc5] = 高塔。她看了很久。“没关系，”她说，“塔会倒。塔就是用来倒的。”
# en: Decline
opt.right.label [eaef39] = 不抽
# en: "Good," she says, putting the deck away. "Knowing is overrated."
opt.right.say.1 [1ff9e2] = “很好。”她把牌收起来，“知道太多被高估了。”

@event seraphine_lake_vision
# en: She Walks Into the Lake
title [7cd453] = 她走进了湖里
# en: From your window you see Seraphine walking into the lake in her nightgown, eyes shining silver, already up to her waist.
text [89cff3] = 你从窗口看见瑟拉芬穿着睡袍走进湖里，眼睛泛着银光，水已经没到了腰。
# en: A girl in a nightgown wading into a misty lake at night, eyes glowing silver, arms outstretched toward something under the water.
scene [21af5a] = 夜里一个穿睡袍的女孩涉入雾气笼罩的湖中，双眼泛着银光，双臂伸向水下的某样东西。
# en: Wake a prefect
opt.left.label [9162cd] = 叫醒一位级长
# en: The prefect drags her out, coughing. She doesn't remember anything. She looks at you strangely for days.
opt.left.say.1 [f25863] = 级长把她拖了出来，她咳个不停。她什么都不记得了。接下来几天，她看你的眼神都怪怪的。
# en: Run down and pull her out
opt.right.label [4787f1] = 冲下去把她拉出来
# en: You reach her just as she goes under. On the shore she wakes and whispers, "It was calling me. It called you too." Then she holds on very tight.
opt.right.say.1 [d29a81] = 她沉下去的那一刻你抓住了她。在岸上，她醒过来低声说：“它在呼唤我。它也呼唤了你。”然后她紧紧抱住了你。
# en: You both nearly drown. You both come down with Lake Fever. She brings you soup that tastes faintly of the future.
opt.right.say.2 [571f07] = 你们俩都差点淹死。你们俩都得了湖热病。她给你送来的汤，隐约有未来的味道。

@event seraphine_future
# en: I Saw You Old
title [9b881b] = 我看见你老了
# en: "I saw you old," Seraphine says suddenly. "Last night. You were happy. Really happy. There was someone with you." She pauses. "Do you want to know who?"
text [c5d67f] = “我看见你老了，”瑟拉芬突然说，“昨晚。你很幸福。真的很幸福。有人陪着你。”她顿了顿，“你想知道是谁吗？”
# en: Two students sitting on the rim of a dry fountain, one looking up at the stars, the other looking at the first with a soft smile.
scene [027150] = 两个学生坐在干涸的喷泉边沿，一个仰望星空，另一个温柔地笑着看向前者。
# en: Yes, tell me
opt.left.label [f7e607] = 想，告诉我
# en: She looks at you for a long time. "I'll tell you when you're old," she says, and goes pink.
opt.left.say.1 [4bb771] = 她看了你很久。“等你老了我再告诉你。”她说，脸红了。
# en: "Someone kind," she says. "That's all I could see. Their hands were kind."
opt.left.say.2 [19f673] = “一个温柔的人，”她说，“我只看得到这么多。那双手很温柔。”
# en: No, let it be a surprise
opt.right.label [97a4ad] = 不了，留个惊喜吧
# en: She smiles like you've given her a present. "That's the right answer. Nobody ever gives the right answer." Not knowing nags at you for days.
opt.right.say.1 [ce9281] = 她笑了，像你送了她一份礼物。“这是正确答案。从来没人给出过正确答案。”不知道答案这件事，让你心痒了好几天。

@event seraphine_overwhelmed
# en: Too Many Tomorrows
title [409210] = 太多个明天
# en: Seraphine hasn't come to class in a week. You find her in a dark storeroom with her hands over her eyes. "It's too loud," she whispers. "Everyone's futures. All at once."
text [92ab7f] = 瑟拉芬已经一周没来上课了。你在一间黑漆漆的储藏室里找到了她，她用双手捂着眼睛。“太吵了，”她低声说，“每个人的未来。一下子全涌过来。”
# en: A girl curled in a dark corner of an observatory with her hands over her eyes, a teacup gone cold beside her.
scene [7f0e93] = 天文台黑暗的角落里蜷缩着一个女孩，双手捂着眼睛，身旁的茶早已凉透。
# en: Fetch Sister Amaranth
opt.left.label [0ebdc9] = 去叫阿玛兰斯修女
# en: Amaranth gives her a sleeping draught and a dark room. She recovers. She doesn't say much about it.
opt.left.say.1 [42cef1] = 阿玛兰斯给了她一剂安眠药和一间暗室。她恢复了。她对此不怎么提起。
# en: Sit with her in the dark
opt.right.label [30debe] = 在黑暗中陪着她
# en: You don't speak. After an hour she takes her hands from her eyes. "Yours is quiet," she says. "Your future. It's very quiet. I like it."
opt.right.say.1 [44b951] = 你没有说话。一个小时后，她把手从眼睛上拿开。“你的很安静，”她说，“你的未来。非常安静。我喜欢。”

@event seraphine_confession
# en: She Already Knew
title [e91972] = 她早就知道
# en: "I've seen this conversation forty-one times," Seraphine says. "In twenty-nine of them, you say yes. I've been very nervous about the other twelve." She holds out her hand. "I like you. That part was always the same."
text [94995b] = “这段对话我已经看过四十一次了，”瑟拉芬说，“其中二十九次你答应了。另外十二次让我很紧张。”她伸出手。“我喜欢你。这一部分每次都一样。”
# en: A girl with silver eyes holding out a single falling-star seed in her palm on a dark observatory balcony.
scene [966292] = 漆黑的天文台阳台上，一个银色眼睛的女孩掌心托着一粒流星的种子递过来。
# en: Gently say no
opt.left.label [f46b92] = 温柔地拒绝
# en: She nods. "Twelve," she says softly. "I knew it might be twelve." She's kind to you afterwards. Somehow that hurts more.
opt.left.say.1 [4e2d00] = 她点点头。“十二，”她轻声说，“我就知道可能是十二。”之后她对你依然很温柔。不知为何，这更让人难过。
# en: Take her hand
opt.right.label [4658a2] = 握住她的手
# en: "Twenty-nine," she whispers, and laughs, and for once she's entirely in the present.
opt.right.say.1 [cd7951] = “二十九。”她低声说，笑了起来，难得地，她完完全全活在当下。

@event corvin_intro
# en: Light Fingers
title [fc7fa5] = 手快
# en: Someone bumps you in the crowd. A moment later a dark-haired boy is bowing and holding up your purse. "You dropped this," he says. "Into my pocket. Terrible habit of yours. Corvin Ashby."
text [88b693] = 人群里有人撞了你一下。片刻之后，一个黑发男生朝你鞠躬，手里举着你的钱袋。“你掉了这个，”他说，“掉进了我的口袋。你这习惯可真糟。科尔文·阿什比。”
# en: A dark-haired student with a crooked grin holding up a purse between two fingers, mid-bow.
scene [77be60] = 一个嘴角歪歪笑着的黑发学生，两指夹着一只钱袋，正弯腰行礼。
# en: Snatch it back and report him
opt.left.label [69c705] = 一把夺回来，举报他
# en: He's gone before the prefect arrives. Your purse is all there, plus an IOU you don't remember receiving.
opt.left.say.1 [2b1b37] = 级长来之前他就不见了。你的钱袋一分不少，只是多了一张你不记得收过的欠条。
# en: Laugh
opt.right.label [52d15e] = 笑出声
# en: "Oh, I like you," he says, and teaches you the trick on the spot. You practise it on him. He lets you win. Probably. Later, you are three crowns short. Probably a coincidence.
opt.right.say.1 [0c1a5b] = “噢，我喜欢你。”他说，当场就把这招教给了你。你拿他练手。他让你赢了。大概吧。后来你发现少了三克朗。大概是巧合。

@event corvin_kitchen_raid
# en: The Kitchen Raid
title [0e6a0c] = 突袭厨房
# en: "Midnight," Corvin whispers. "The cooks have made forty treacle tarts for the faculty dinner. Forty. Nobody needs forty."
text [ccccc4] = “午夜，”科尔文低声说，“厨师们给教职员晚宴做了四十个糖浆馅饼。四十个。没人需要四十个。”
# en: Two students creeping through a cavernous castle kitchen at night, a mountain of tarts on a table, a sleeping cook snoring by the hearth.
scene [c71678] = 夜里两个学生蹑手蹑脚地穿过城堡里洞穴般的大厨房，桌上堆着小山一样的馅饼，炉边的厨师打着呼噜。
# en: Not tonight
opt.left.label [4bf72b] = 今晚不行
# en: He goes alone. The next morning there's a treacle tart on your pillow. You decide not to ask.
opt.left.say.1 [4aa606] = 他自己去了。第二天早上你的枕头上放着一个糖浆馅饼。你决定不问。
# en: Lead the raid
opt.right.label [a419e4] = 带头突袭
# en: You get out with nine tarts and a bottle of elderflower cordial. You eat them on the roof until sunrise.
opt.right.say.1 [f86666] = 你们带着九个馅饼和一瓶接骨木花露溜了出来。在屋顶上一直吃到日出。
# en: The cook wakes up. You both spend a week scrubbing pans, laughing too hard to work.
opt.right.say.2 [eb0bd4] = 厨师醒了。你们俩刷了一星期的锅，笑得根本干不动活。

@event corvin_debt
# en: Corvin's Little Problem
title [7d9f5d] = 科尔文的小麻烦
# en: Corvin has a black eye and a very casual expression. "Small misunderstanding with some trolls," he says. "Thirty crowns would clear it right up. I'll pay you back. Probably with interest. Possibly with a goat."
text [6c578d] = 科尔文顶着一只黑眼圈，表情非常随意。“和几个巨魔有点小误会，”他说，“三十克朗就能摆平。我会还你的。大概还带利息。也可能带一只山羊。”
# en: A boy with a black eye sitting on the dormitory stairs, trying very hard to look casual.
scene [720349] = 一个顶着黑眼圈的男生坐在宿舍楼梯上，非常努力地装作若无其事。
# en: Refuse
opt.left.label [cada35] = 拒绝
# en: "Course. No problem." He has another black eye the next week. He's still friendly. Mostly.
opt.left.say.1 [71b32c] = “当然。没问题。”下周他又多了一只黑眼圈。他对你依然友好。大体上。
# en: Give him thirty crowns
opt.right.label [902ad2] = 给他三十克朗
# en: He stares at the coins, then at you. "No one's ever just... done that." He's quiet for a whole minute. A record.
opt.right.say.1 [9d7807] = 他盯着硬币，又盯着你。“从来没有人就这么……给过。”他安静了整整一分钟。破纪录了。

@event corvin_repays
# en: Interest
title [8f88f3] = 利息
# en: There's a fat purse on your desk and a jack of spades tucked under it. It's heavy, and it clinks.
text [5a0eec] = 你桌上放着一只鼓鼓的钱袋，下面压着一张黑桃 J。沉甸甸的，叮当作响。
# en: A small brass key and a fat purse left on a desk with a playing card, the jack of spades, tucked under them.
scene [476a3b] = 桌上放着一把黄铜小钥匙和一只鼓鼓的钱袋，下面压着一张扑克牌——黑桃 J。
# en: Count it
opt.left.label [5fce81] = 数一数
# en: Sixty crowns. A note: "Interest. Don't ask. — C." You don't ask.
opt.left.say.1 [f9e2eb] = 六十克朗。一张字条：“利息。别问。——科”你没问。
# en: Three crowns and a very convincing IOU for the other twenty-seven, with a doodle of a goat.
opt.left.say.2 [8ec290] = 三克朗，外加一张写着剩下二十七克朗、非常有说服力的欠条，上面还画了只山羊。
# en: Find him and ask where it came from
opt.right.label [397662] = 找到他，问钱哪儿来的
# en: "I won it," he says. "Fairly. Mostly." He pushes the exact thirty into your hand. "The rest's mine. I've got another debt to pay."
opt.right.say.1 [efb600] = “赢来的，”他说，“公平地。大体上。”他把正好三十克朗塞进你手里。“剩下的是我的。我还有另一笔债要还。”

@event corvin_rooftop
# en: Up on the Roof
title [6ebee8] = 屋顶上
# en: On the roof at 2am, Corvin goes quiet. "I'm on my last warning," he says. "One more detention and they send me home. And home is... not a good place." He laughs, badly.
text [dc6f28] = 凌晨两点的屋顶上，科尔文沉默了下来。“我已经是最后一次警告了，”他说，“再关一次禁闭，他们就送我回家。而家……不是个好地方。”他笑了，笑得很难看。
# en: Two students sitting on a steep slate roof under a full moon, legs dangling over a dizzying drop, sharing a bottle of something fizzy.
scene [802031] = 满月下两个学生坐在陡峭的石板屋顶上，双腿悬在令人眩晕的高处，分享着一瓶冒泡的饮料。
# en: Tell him to keep his head down
opt.left.label [b7afec] = 叫他低调点
# en: "Head down. Right. I'll try anything once." He keeps his head down for almost a month.
opt.left.say.1 [199c3a] = “低调。好。什么我都愿意试一次。”他低调了将近一个月。
# en: Promise you'll cover for him
opt.right.label [f74b9c] = 保证会帮他打掩护
# en: He looks at you like nobody has ever promised him anything. "You're an idiot," he says. "Thank you."
opt.right.say.1 [34b1d4] = 他看着你，好像从没有人给过他任何承诺。“你是个傻瓜，”他说，“谢谢你。”

@event corvin_framed
# en: Corvin Is Framed
title [bd8e3b] = 科尔文被陷害了
# en: The headmistress's silver goblet has been found in Corvin's trunk. He swears he didn't take it. Bram, who found it, looks very pleased. Corvin is one detention from expulsion.
text [7254e4] = 院长的银高脚杯在科尔文的行李箱里被找到了。他发誓不是他拿的。发现它的布拉姆看起来非常得意。科尔文离被开除只差一次禁闭。
# en: A boy standing before a disciplinary desk, a stolen silver goblet on it, a smug prefect at his shoulder.
scene [c0253d] = 一个男生站在纪律桌前，桌上放着一只失窃的银高脚杯，一个得意的级长站在他肩旁。
# en: Stay out of it
opt.left.label [03d24a] = 不掺和
# en: Corvin talks his way out, barely. He doesn't look at you for a month.
opt.left.say.1 [90a1f1] = 科尔文勉强靠嘴皮子脱了身。他一个月没正眼看你。
# en: Corvin is suspended for a month. When he comes back, he's different. Quieter.
opt.left.say.2 [506649] = 科尔文被停学一个月。回来时，他变了。更沉默了。
# en: Find proof he was framed
opt.right.label [0665b1] = 找出他被陷害的证据
# en: You find the bill of sale: Bram bought a fake. Bram is stripped of his sash for the rest of the year. Corvin buys you a goat. An actual goat.
opt.right.say.1 [e722b3] = 你找到了那张收据：是布拉姆买了个赝品。布拉姆被摘掉了绶带，这一年都别想再戴。科尔文送了你一只山羊。真的山羊。
# en: You can't prove it. But you stood up for him in front of everyone, and he'll never forget it. Neither will Bram.
opt.right.say.2 [1b083f] = 你证明不了。但你当着所有人的面为他站了出来，他永远不会忘记。布拉姆也不会。

@event corvin_confession
# en: Corvin, Serious for Once
title [4a31ce] = 难得认真的科尔文
# en: Corvin holds out a playing card. The queen of hearts. His hand isn't quite steady. "No trick," he says. "No angle. I just — I like you more than I like anything, and I'm terrified, and I wanted you to have this."
text [87fdba] = 科尔文递过来一张扑克牌。红桃 Q。他的手有点不稳。“没有把戏，”他说，“没有算计。我只是——我喜欢你，胜过喜欢任何东西，我怕得要命，而且我想把这个给你。”
# en: A boy holding out a playing card — the queen of hearts — with an unsteady hand, no grin for once.
scene [e450dd] = 一个男生用不太稳的手递出一张扑克牌——红桃 Q——这一次他没有笑。
# en: Gently decline
opt.left.label [975956] = 温柔地拒绝
# en: He laughs, too quickly. "Worth a shot." He keeps the card. You see it sometimes, tucked in his sleeve.
opt.left.say.1 [cd0293] = 他笑了，笑得太快。“值得一试。”他留着那张牌。你有时会看见它藏在他的袖子里。
# en: Take the card
opt.right.label [e7f785] = 接过那张牌
# en: For once, Corvin Ashby has nothing to say. He just kisses you, and then grins, and then can't stop grinning.
opt.right.say.1 [108f24] = 科尔文·阿什比难得地无话可说。他只是吻了你，然后咧嘴笑，然后再也停不下来。

@event corvin_runaway
# en: Let's Leave Tonight
title [03c686] = 今晚就走吧
# en: Corvin's at your door at midnight, bag over his shoulder. "There's a sky-barge at the dock and nobody guarding it. Let's go. Tonight. The world's huge and we're wasting it in classrooms."
text [c8d466] = 午夜，科尔文背着包站在你门口。“码头上停着一艘天空驳船，没人看守。走吧。今晚。世界那么大，我们却在教室里浪费它。”
# en: A small sky-barge tied to the academy dock at midnight, lanterns lit, a boy at the tiller holding out his hand.
scene [6e8955] = 午夜时分，一艘小天空驳船系在学院码头上，灯笼亮着，一个男生站在舵边向你伸出手。
# en: Stay and finish what you started
opt.left.label [6b504c] = 留下来，把开始的事做完
# en: He looks at you for a long time. Then he drops the bag. "Fine. But after graduation, we steal a boat. A big one."
opt.left.say.1 [d46286] = 他看了你很久。然后放下了包。“行。但毕业以后，我们去偷条船。一条大的。”
# en: Take his hand
opt.right.label [0c017b] = 握住他的手

@event mir_intro
# en: An Explosion in the West Wing
title [dbebf9] = 西翼爆炸
# en: The west wing explodes. Not badly. A figure in goggles stumbles out of the purple smoke, coughing, and gives you a thumbs-up. "Don't worry! That was intentional! Mostly! Can you hold this?" They hand you a ticking teapot.
text [61d334] = 西翼炸了。不严重。一个戴护目镜的身影咳嗽着从紫烟里踉跄出来，冲你竖起大拇指。“别担心！是故意的！大体上！能帮我拿一下这个吗？”TA递给你一只滴答作响的茶壶。
# en: A cloud of purple smoke billowing from a workshop door, a soot-covered student emerging with goggles and a thumbs-up.
scene [6592e9] = 一团紫烟从工坊门口滚滚涌出，一个满身煤灰、戴着护目镜的学生走出来竖起大拇指。
# en: Put the teapot down and back away
opt.left.label [0e8c08] = 放下茶壶，往后退
# en: The teapot stops ticking and starts humming the academy anthem. "Mir," they say. "They/them. Thanks for not throwing it."
opt.left.say.1 [e3a008] = 茶壶停止了滴答，开始哼起院歌。“米尔，”TA说，“代词用 TA。谢谢你没把它扔出去。”
# en: Hold the teapot steady
opt.right.label [74455a] = 稳稳端住茶壶
# en: You keep it level while they twist a valve. It stops ticking. "You've got good hands," Mir says. "I'm going to need those."
opt.right.say.1 [ce47f9] = 你端平茶壶，TA拧了拧一个阀门。滴答声停了。“你的手很稳，”米尔说，“我会需要这双手的。”
# en: The teapot goes off. Your eyebrows survive, mostly. Mir is apologising and laughing at the same time.
opt.right.say.2 [3dba78] = 茶壶炸了。你的眉毛基本保住了。米尔一边道歉一边笑。

@event mir_owl_gift
# en: A Present With Gears
title [940c6d] = 带齿轮的礼物
# en: Mir presents a brass owl with amber glass eyes. It blinks, hoots the hour and says "HOMEWORK" in a tinny voice. "Made it for you. It remembers deadlines. And birthdays. And grudges, slightly."
text [1b3dc2] = 米尔拿出一只长着琥珀玻璃眼睛的黄铜猫头鹰。它眨眨眼，报了时，然后用细细的声音说：“作业。”“给你做的。它会记住截止日期。还有生日。还有一点点仇。”
# en: A small brass owl with glowing amber eyes perched on a student's wrist, its clockwork feathers fluffing.
scene [0ec99d] = 一只长着发光琥珀眼睛的小黄铜猫头鹰栖在学生的手腕上，发条羽毛蓬松起来。
# en: It's too much
opt.left.label [8c1449] = 这太贵重了
# en: Mir looks crushed, then rallies. "I'll give it to Thorne. He needs reminding to smile." The owl, you hear, refuses to work for him.
opt.left.say.1 [b9afa1] = 米尔一脸受伤，随即振作起来。“那我送给索恩。他需要有人提醒他笑一笑。”你听说，那只猫头鹰拒绝为他工作。
# en: Accept it gratefully
opt.right.label [0fb4bf] = 感激地收下
# en: The owl settles on your shoulder and says, "WELCOME." Mir pretends to have something in their eye. At six the next morning, the owl says "HOMEWORK." It says it every morning for the rest of the year.
opt.right.say.1 [4cd7a1] = 猫头鹰落在你肩上，说：“欢迎。”米尔假装眼睛里进了东西。第二天早上六点，猫头鹰说：“作业。”接下来的一整年，它每天早上都这么说。

@event mir_fair
# en: The Artificers' Fair
title [e5694f] = 奇械博览会
# en: The Artificers' Fair. Mir's entry is under a sheet and occasionally growls. "I need an assistant to stand next to it and look confident," they say. "And possibly run."
text [f589cf] = 奇械博览会。米尔的参赛作品盖在一块布下，时不时发出低吼。“我需要一个助手站在它旁边，看起来很自信，”TA说，“可能还需要跑。”
# en: A hall crammed with bizarre inventions — walking teapots, singing clocks — and one enormous brass machine draped in a sheet.
scene [63de4d] = 大厅里挤满了千奇百怪的发明——会走路的茶壶、会唱歌的钟——还有一台盖着布的巨大黄铜机器。
# en: Watch from a safe distance
opt.left.label [5c0ef7] = 在安全距离外观看
# en: The machine turns out to be a mechanical bear that bakes bread. It wins second place. Mir is ecstatic and flour-covered.
opt.left.say.1 [f14a15] = 那台机器原来是一只会烤面包的机械熊。它拿了二等奖。米尔欣喜若狂，满身面粉。
# en: Be the confident assistant
opt.right.label [bfb41b] = 当那个自信的助手
# en: You present it like a showman. The bear bakes a perfect loaf and bows. First prize. Mir kisses the trophy, then, in a fluster, your cheek.
opt.right.say.1 [cb3cfc] = 你像个表演家一样介绍它。熊烤出一条完美的面包，还鞠了一躬。一等奖。米尔亲了一下奖杯，然后慌慌张张地，亲了一下你的脸颊。
# en: The bear eats your sleeve and swats you into the flour bins on its way to the judges. The crowd loves it. Third prize and a very good story.
opt.right.say.2 [6f8c14] = 熊吃了你的袖子，在走向评委的路上还把你一巴掌拍进了面粉桶。观众爱死了。三等奖，外加一个特别好的故事。

@event mir_workshop_closed
# en: The Workshop Is Shut
title [61b17b] = 工坊被封了
# en: After the third fire this term, the faculty has padlocked Mir's workshop. Mir is sitting on a toolbox outside it, looking like someone took their heart and filed it under "hazards".
text [f5f0a5] = 这学期第三场火灾之后，学院给米尔的工坊上了锁。米尔坐在门外的工具箱上，看起来像有人把TA的心拿走，归档到了“危险品”一栏。
# en: A workshop door chained shut with a faculty notice nailed to it, a forlorn student sitting on a toolbox outside.
scene [d57061] = 一扇被铁链锁住的工坊门，上面钉着学院告示，一个失魂落魄的学生坐在门外的工具箱上。
# en: Plead their case to Professor Thorne
opt.left.label [fa15a7] = 向索恩教授求情
# en: Thorne agrees to reopen it — with fire buckets and a weekly inspection. Mir cries on you. Oil and all.
opt.left.say.1 [f9ab11] = 索恩同意重新开放——条件是配备消防桶并每周检查。米尔抱着你哭了。连油带泪。
# en: Thorne refuses. But Mir heard you try. "Nobody's ever argued for me before," they say.
opt.left.say.2 [d56047] = 索恩拒绝了。但米尔听到了你的争取。“从来没有人替我争过。”TA说。
# en: Help them build a secret workshop
opt.right.label [4db846] = 帮TA建一个秘密工坊
# en: An abandoned classroom behind a tapestry. You bring candles; Mir brings everything else. It's perfect. It's almost entirely fireproof.
opt.right.say.1 [090930] = 挂毯后面一间废弃的教室。你带来了蜡烛；米尔带来了其他所有东西。完美。而且几乎完全防火。
# en: Bram finds the secret workshop on day two. Worth it, says Mir, scrubbing cauldrons beside you.
opt.right.say.2 [f9bf9c] = 第二天布拉姆就发现了秘密工坊。值了，米尔一边在你旁边刷坩埚一边说。

@event mir_dance_machine
# en: The Dancing Machine
title [88d879] = 跳舞机
# en: Mir has built a machine that teaches dancing. It has six legs and opinions. "It needs a test subject," they say. "It's mostly safe. It only kicked me twice."
text [afec3b] = 米尔造了一台教人跳舞的机器。它有六条腿，还有自己的主见。“它需要一个测试对象，”TA说，“基本上是安全的。它只踢了我两次。”
# en: A spindly brass contraption with too many legs attempting a waltz in an empty classroom, a student dancing with it.
scene [76ab76] = 空荡荡的教室里，一台腿太多的细长黄铜装置正试图跳华尔兹，一个学生在和它共舞。
# en: Make Mir test it
opt.left.label [78abd6] = 让米尔自己测
# en: You watch Mir and the machine waltz, badly, across the room. It kicks them twice; Mir gives you a look. It's the funniest thing you've ever seen.
opt.left.say.1 [e8b145] = 你看着米尔和机器笨拙地在教室里跳华尔兹。它踢了米尔两脚；米尔瞪了你一眼。这是你见过最好笑的事。
# en: Dance with the machine
opt.right.label [39f27e] = 和机器跳舞
# en: It kicks you twice too. But by the end you can waltz, and Mir is clapping with oily hands.
opt.right.say.1 [4fe4d1] = 它也踢了你两次。但最后你学会了华尔兹，米尔用满是油污的手鼓着掌。

@event mir_confession
# en: Blueprint
title [680200] = 蓝图
# en: Mir unrolls a blueprint. It's a mechanical heart, labelled in tiny careful handwriting: "Does not work without the other part." They clear their throat. "I'm bad at saying things. So I drew it. You're the other part. If you want."
text [f59e74] = 米尔展开一张蓝图。上面是一颗机械心脏，用细小工整的字迹标注着：“缺少另一个部件时无法运转。”TA清了清嗓子。“我不擅长说话。所以我画了出来。你就是那个部件。如果你愿意的话。”
# en: A rolled-out blueprint on a workbench showing a heart-shaped mechanism labelled with tiny careful notes, a nervous artificer beside it.
scene [4f0a67] = 工作台上展开一张蓝图，画着心形机械装置并标满细小工整的注释，旁边站着一个紧张的奇械师。
# en: Kindly say no
opt.left.label [304162] = 委婉地拒绝
# en: Mir rolls up the blueprint carefully. "Good to know. Data is data." They're fine. They're mostly fine.
opt.left.say.1 [457a7a] = 米尔小心地卷起蓝图。“知道了。数据就是数据。”TA没事。TA基本上没事。
# en: "I want."
opt.right.label [12191a] = “我愿意。”
# en: The heart doesn't need to work. But Mir builds it anyway, and it ticks on your windowsill, in time with your own.
opt.right.say.1 [7bae7b] = 那颗心不需要真的运转。但米尔还是把它造了出来，它在你的窗台上滴答作响，与你的心跳同拍。

@event mir_family_business
# en: The Family Clockworks
title [a29c6c] = 家族钟表行
# en: A letter from Mir's parents: the family clockworks needs them home. A ticket is enclosed. "They think this is a hobby," Mir says. "This. Is. Not. A. Hobby."
text [51cd75] = 米尔父母来信：家族钟表行需要TA回家。信里附了一张车票。“他们以为这是兴趣爱好，”米尔说，“这。不是。兴趣。爱好。”
# en: An artificer holding a stiff letter embossed with a gear crest, a train ticket tucked inside, staring at it blankly.
scene [2991ee] = 一个奇械师拿着一封印有齿轮家徽的硬挺信件，里面夹着一张车票，茫然地盯着它。
# en: Tell them family comes first
opt.left.label [170ef7] = 告诉TA家人最重要
# en: Mir goes home for a month and comes back with a new scar and a clearer jaw. "They know now," they say. "It's not a hobby. You were right to send me."
opt.left.say.1 [68c5b3] = 米尔回家待了一个月，回来时多了一道新疤，下颌线也更坚定了。“他们现在知道了，”TA说，“这不是兴趣爱好。你让我回去是对的。”
# en: Help them write back
opt.right.label [7d4c22] = 帮TA写回信
# en: Together you spend three evenings, and most of your coursework, on a letter so persuasive it should be framed. Mir's mother replies: "Fine. Win a prize." Mir intends to win all of them.
opt.right.say.1 [e7acb4] = 你们一起花了三个晚上，搭进去大半功课，写了一封有说服力到该裱起来的信。米尔的母亲回信：“好吧。拿个奖回来。”米尔打算把所有奖都拿回来。

@event nessa_intro
# en: First Impressions
title [eee0a7] = 第一印象
# en: A girl with a quill floating at her shoulder plants herself in front of you. "Nessa Quill, Lumen Ledger. First impressions of Lumenhold, go. Be interesting, please. The last six were boring."
text [569607] = 一个肩头飘着羽毛笔的女孩往你面前一站。“内莎·奎尔，《流明纪事报》。对流明堡的第一印象，说吧。拜托说点有意思的。前六个都很无聊。”
# en: A girl with ink-stained fingers and a self-writing quill floating at her shoulder, holding a notebook out expectantly.
scene [e133f9] = 一个手指沾满墨迹的女孩，肩头飘着一支自动羽毛笔，满怀期待地递出笔记本。
# en: Give a safe answer
opt.left.label [6b761a] = 给个稳妥的回答
# en: The quill writes "SAFE" in the margin and underlines it twice. Nessa sighs and moves on.
opt.left.say.1 [9dd6db] = 羽毛笔在页边写下“稳妥”，还划了两道线。内莎叹了口气，走向下一个人。
# en: Say something outrageous
opt.right.label [9ecd42] = 说点惊人之语
# en: You're quoted on the front page. Half the academy now thinks you're hilarious. The other half thinks you're dangerous. Nessa thinks both.
opt.right.say.1 [83d022] = 你上了头版。现在半个学院觉得你很搞笑。另一半觉得你很危险。内莎觉得两者都是。
# en: You are quoted. Out of context. Extremely out of context.
opt.right.say.2 [8af99f] = 你被引用了。断章取义了。极其断章取义。

@event nessa_gossip_column
# en: You're in the Gossip Column
title [22e6ad] = 你上了八卦专栏
# en: This week's Ledger gossip column features you, prominently, under the headline "WHO IS THE MYSTERY STUDENT ALWAYS IN THE LIBRARY AT MIDNIGHT?" Nessa swears she didn't write it.
text [6890e5] = 本周《纪事报》的八卦专栏以醒目的标题刊登了你：“总在午夜出现在图书馆的神秘学生是谁？”内莎发誓不是她写的。
# en: A copy of the Lumen Ledger pinned to a noticeboard, a gossip column circled in red ink, students gathered round giggling.
scene [ab1073] = 布告栏上钉着一份《流明纪事报》，八卦专栏被红墨水圈了出来，学生们围在一起咯咯笑。
# en: Confront Nessa
opt.left.label [e29ecc] = 找内莎对质
# en: She prints a correction. Sort of. It's a much more flattering paragraph about you.
opt.left.say.1 [4756b3] = 她登了一则更正。算是吧。是一段把你夸得天花乱坠的文字。
# en: "Freedom of the press," says Nessa, sweetly. You both know she wrote it.
opt.left.say.2 [8b1a52] = “新闻自由。”内莎甜甜地说。你们都知道是她写的。
# en: Lean into the mystery
opt.right.label [0d58af] = 顺水推舟，故弄玄虚
# en: You start leaving cryptic notes in the library. The column runs for six more weeks. Nessa is delighted.
opt.right.say.1 [ddffb0] = 你开始在图书馆里留下神秘的字条。这个专栏又连载了六周。内莎乐坏了。
# en: The column runs for six more weeks. By the fourth it has decided you are haunting the library, and people move tables when you sit down.
opt.right.say.2 [524d7e] = 专栏又连载了六周。到第四周，它认定你在图书馆闹鬼，你一坐下，别人就换桌子。

@event nessa_source
# en: The Source
title [86f411] = 线人
# en: Nessa leans in. "You've got faculty access. The professors are planning to change the exam format and they're hiding it. I just need a quote. Anonymous. Please?"
text [9e9d3b] = 内莎凑过来。“你能接触到教职员。教授们打算改考试形式，还瞒着大家。我只需要一句引述。匿名的。拜托？”
# en: Two students in a dark corner of the library, one whispering, the other writing furiously in a notebook.
scene [7686b3] = 图书馆昏暗的角落里两个学生，一个在低语，另一个在笔记本上奋笔疾书。
# en: Refuse — that's a breach of trust
opt.left.label [a7260f] = 拒绝——这是背信
# en: Nessa sulks for a day. Then she respects you for it, which she hates. You sleep well.
opt.left.say.1 [06a158] = 内莎生了一天闷气。然后她因此尊重你，这让她很恼火。你睡得很安稳。
# en: Give her the scoop
opt.right.label [3204b4] = 把独家消息给她
# en: The story runs. Thorne knows exactly who talked. His glare could curdle milk.
opt.right.say.1 [019448] = 报道刊出了。索恩完全清楚是谁说出去的。他的瞪视能让牛奶结块。
# en: The story runs. Students are grateful. Nobody knows it was you. Nessa buys you cake.
opt.right.say.2 [baa867] = 报道刊出了。学生们心怀感激。没人知道是你。内莎请你吃了蛋糕。

@event nessa_hollow_story
# en: Nessa Smells a Story
title [9fa969] = 内莎嗅到了新闻
# en: Nessa's office wall is covered in red string. In the middle: a sketch of a black star. "Frozen fountains. Missing pages. A transfer from the North. Something's going on and you know about it. Spill."
text [f90ecc] = 内莎办公室的墙上缠满了红线。正中间：一幅黑星的速写。“结冰的喷泉。失踪的书页。一个从北方来的转学生。有什么事正在发生，而你知道内情。说吧。”
# en: A wall in the newspaper office covered in pinned clippings and red string connecting a frozen lake, a black star and a fur-coated boy.
scene [320fce] = 报社墙上钉满剪报，红线连接着冰封的湖、一颗黑星和一个穿毛皮大衣的少年。
# en: Warn her off — it's dangerous
opt.left.label [deabae] = 劝她收手——太危险了
# en: "That's what people say right before the best stories." But she takes the string down. Mostly.
opt.left.say.1 [448d70] = “大家都是在最好的新闻出现之前这么说的。”但她还是把红线拆了。大部分。
# en: Share what you know
opt.right.label [6ba460] = 告诉她你知道的
# en: Nessa's article runs with half the facts. The man in grey reads it. So does Bram, who starts following you around.
opt.right.say.1 [84698a] = 内莎的文章只登出了一半事实。灰衣人读到了。布拉姆也读到了，他开始到处跟着你。
# en: Nessa's notes are scarily thorough. She's found a record of three students who vanished in 1723. All on Blossom moons.
opt.right.say.2 [ab1477] = 内莎的笔记详尽得吓人。她找到了一份记录：1723 年有三个学生失踪。全都在花潮之月。

@event nessa_paper_threatened
# en: Stop the Presses
title [447c01] = 停印
# en: The headmistress has threatened to shut down the Ledger after an article about faculty salaries. Nessa is organising a protest. "I need people on the steps. Visible people. You."
text [2ab439] = 一篇关于教职员薪水的文章刊出后，院长威胁要关停《纪事报》。内莎正在组织抗议。“我需要有人站在台阶上。显眼的人。你。”
# en: A printing press with a faculty seal stamped across it, a defiant student standing in front of it with arms crossed.
scene [94267d] = 一台被盖上学院封印的印刷机，一个倔强的学生抱着双臂站在它前面。
# en: Stay out of it
opt.left.label [03d24a] = 不掺和
# en: The protest is small. The Ledger survives, barely. Nessa notices who wasn't there.
opt.left.say.1 [98928f] = 抗议规模很小。《纪事报》勉强保住了。内莎记住了谁没来。
# en: Stand on the steps
opt.right.label [1c328c] = 站上台阶
# en: Forty students on the steps, chanting. The headmistress comes out and, astonishingly, listens, looking straight at you the whole time, and not warmly. The Ledger stays.
opt.right.say.1 [adae4f] = 四十个学生站在台阶上高呼口号。院长走了出来，出人意料地，她听了，而且自始至终直直地看着你，目光并不温和。《纪事报》保住了。

@event nessa_confession
# en: Off the Record
title [a5d3b6] = 不予记录
# en: Nessa puts down her quill. Then she tells it to stop writing. It's the first time you've seen it still. "This is off the record," she says. "Completely. I like you. I've drafted this eleven times. None of the drafts were good enough."
text [b22faa] = 内莎放下了羽毛笔。然后命令它停止书写。这是你第一次看见它静止不动。“这段不予记录，”她说，“完全不记。我喜欢你。这段话我打了十一遍草稿。没有一稿够好。”
# en: A girl with an inkpot in one hand, her self-writing quill hovering above a blank page that she has commanded to stay blank.
scene [b44415] = 一个女孩一手拿着墨水瓶，她的自动羽毛笔悬在一张空白的纸上方——她命令那张纸保持空白。
# en: Gently say no
opt.left.label [f46b92] = 温柔地拒绝
# en: "Noted," she says crisply. She keeps her quill still a moment longer. Then it starts writing again, and so does she.
opt.left.say.1 [3ad266] = “记下了。”她干脆地说。她让羽毛笔多静止了一会儿。然后它重新开始书写，她也是。
# en: Kiss her
opt.right.label [5fa79c] = 吻她
# en: Her quill, unattended, writes a single word in the margin: "FINALLY."
opt.right.say.1 [995169] = 无人看管的羽毛笔在页边写下了两个字：“终于。”
